E_S3_NOT_CONFIGURED	409	https://docs.fleetly.dev/errors/E_S3_NOT_CONFIGURED	a service declares label fleetly.s3=true but object storage is not configured (s3.mode=unset); deploy plan refuses instead of injecting empty env	Configure object storage first: run 'fleetly s3 set' (or the Console S3 settings card) to set s3.mode=external or rustfs, then deploy again.	E3 object-storage §5.2 (label-injection sentinel; wired with E3-4)
E_S3_PUBLIC_REQUIRES_BASE_DOMAIN	409	https://docs.fleetly.dev/errors/E_S3_PUBLIC_REQUIRES_BASE_DOMAIN	s3.public_exposed requires a platform base domain (public subdomain s3.<base> derivation); refused in the single-node form without one	Configure base_domain (installer --base-domain) before exposing RustFS on the public subdomain s3.<base>; keep public_exposed=false for internal-only access.	E3 object-storage §5.2 (public subdomain toggle without a base domain)
E_S3_TEST_FAILED	503	https://docs.fleetly.dev/errors/E_S3_TEST_FAILED	S3 connection test failed (probe put→get→delete; the failed step and the underlying error travel in the envelope context; this is a reachable-endpoint fault, not a TCP probe)	Fix the endpoint/credentials per the failed probe step (put=auth/write, get=readback, delete=cleanup) and test again; the honest contract is: test passed = can authenticate, can write, can read back.	E3 object-storage §5.2 (connection probe failed; failed step in the envelope context)
E_SCHEDULER_PENDING_TIMEOUT	500	https://docs.fleetly.dev/errors/E_SCHEDULER_PENDING_TIMEOUT	task stuck in PENDING past the deploy watchdog (placement constraints/insufficient resources/node unavailable)	Check node resources and placement constraints (whether the bound node is ready); free resources or adjust constraints and retry.	release-semantics §2.7
E_SECRET_NOT_FOUND	422	https://docs.fleetly.dev/errors/E_SECRET_NOT_FOUND	a compose-declared external secret is not in the platform secret store (deploy preflight)	Create the secret first (fleetly secrets set) with the exact declared name, then deploy again; compose secrets must declare external: true.	E4 managed-databases §5.2 (compose-declared external secret missing; preflight)
E_STATE_VERSION_CONFLICT	409	https://docs.fleetly.dev/errors/E_STATE_VERSION_CONFLICT	read-before-write optimistic concurrency conflict (object version token invalid)	The object was modified concurrently: re-read the latest state and retry with the new version token.	state-model §2.2 (same as architecture §2.3)
E_TASK_QUOTA_EXCEEDED	429	https://docs.fleetly.dev/errors/E_TASK_QUOTA_EXCEEDED	the token's task quota is exhausted (concurrent tasks or total CPU/memory of non-terminal tasks at the limit; fail-closed)	Wait for running tasks to reach a terminal state (TTL reclaim or explicit stop) before creating more, or raise the per-token quota.	T-line DT-5/IMPL-T2-1 (per-token concurrent/resource quota exhausted; fail-closed at CreateTask, 429)
E_TASK_START_FAILED	500	https://docs.fleetly.dev/errors/E_TASK_START_FAILED	new task failed to start (image entrypoint/resource limits/runtime error)	Check the task logs to locate the start failure, fix it, and retry.	release-semantics §2.7
E_TASK_UNSUPPORTED	400	https://docs.fleetly.dev/errors/E_TASK_UNSUPPORTED	task request falls outside the dynamic-workload contract (scope kind/ref invalid, internal variant unsupported for the scope kind, scope network absent, ttl/resource bounds violated)	Fix the named field: internal=true is only supported for task-group networks; tasks join networks that already exist (create the task-group network via EnsureTaskNetwork first); ttl_seconds must be within [60, 86400] and resources within the platform bounds.	T-line DT-5/IMPL-T2-1 (task scope/internal variant/ttl/resource bounds violated; tasks join existing networks only, 400)
E_TEAM_LAST_OWNER	409	https://docs.fleetly.dev/errors/E_TEAM_LAST_OWNER	last-team-owner guard: removing or demoting the only owner would leave the team without a responsible party	Grant the owner role to another member first (POST /v1/teams/{team_id}/members:set-role), then retry; a team always keeps at least one owner.	v0.3 W2-S1 rbac-teams §3.1/§5 (last-team-owner guard on member removal/demotion, 409)
E_TEAM_SLUG_RESERVED	422	https://docs.fleetly.dev/errors/E_TEAM_SLUG_RESERVED	the team slug collides with a platform-reserved component name (v0.3 naming formulas derive fleetly-<team>-* objects from the team slug; the reserved set guards the prefix families)	Pick another slug outside the reserved set (listed in the error message); slugs are lowercase word-form identifiers [a-z0-9]{2,32} and immutable once created.	v0.3 W2-S1 rbac-teams §4.3/§5 (team slug vs platform component namespaces — v0.3 naming formulas take the team slug as parameter, 422)
E_TERMINAL_DISABLED	409	https://docs.fleetly.dev/errors/E_TERMINAL_DISABLED	the web terminal feature is disabled (terminal.enabled=false): no exec relay is deployed and no terminal tickets are issued	Enable the feature by setting terminal.enabled: true in the control plane config and restarting fleetlyd; the exec relay manager converges the fleetly-exec service on every node automatically.	E7 web-terminal §2.4 (W5-S6 feature gate: terminal.enabled=false deploys no exec relay and refuses ticket issuance, 409)
E_TOKEN_LAST_ADMIN	409	https://docs.fleetly.dev/errors/E_TOKEN_LAST_ADMIN	last-admin guard: revoking would leave no unrevoked admin token on the platform; self-lockout rejected	This is the last unrevoked admin token: create a new admin token before revoking this one (otherwise the platform becomes unmanageable, and the bootstrap token is not reseeded on restart).	M4-6 added during implementation (review remediation B5: token last-admin guard; pending T0.5 freeze confirmation)
E_VOLUME_NODE_MISMATCH	409	https://docs.fleetly.dev/errors/E_VOLUME_NODE_MISMATCH	volume data node ≠ target deploy node (data-safety sentinel that turns the empty-volume incident into a 409)	Declare a data disposition and retry: --data-restored (rebuilt by the restore flow) or --discard (admin+confirm; the old volume becomes orphaned).	stateful-placement §2.8
E_WEBHOOK_NAME_CONFLICT	409	https://docs.fleetly.dev/errors/E_WEBHOOK_NAME_CONFLICT	a webhook endpoint with the same name already exists (endpoint names are unique)	Pick another endpoint name (or delete the old endpoint first); names are the operator-facing handle used by the CLI and Console.	E6 observability §5 (W5-S4 endpoint names are unique: envelope projection of the state sentinel, 409)
E_WEBHOOK_NOT_FOUND	404	https://docs.fleetly.dev/errors/E_WEBHOOK_NOT_FOUND	the webhook endpoint referenced by the operation does not exist (or was already deleted)	List the endpoints with 'fleetly notifications endpoint list' and retry with an existing name or id. Deleting an endpoint also removes its delivery ledger rows.	E6 observability §5 (W5-S4 webhook endpoint absent: envelope projection of the state sentinel, 404)
E_WEBHOOK_PATTERN_INVALID	422	https://docs.fleetly.dev/errors/E_WEBHOOK_PATTERN_INVALID	a webhook event pattern is invalid (patterns must be a non-empty list of 1..128 chars from [a-z0-9._-*]; '*' is the wildcard)	Use event-name glob patterns like "deployment.*", "cron.failed" or "*" (matches everything); see 'fleetly events watch' for the event vocabulary the patterns match against.	E6 observability §5 (W5-S4 subscription glob pattern rejected by the whitelist: non-empty [a-z0-9._-*], 422)
W_DEPLOY_INSTABILITY	0	https://docs.fleetly.dev/errors/W_DEPLOY_INSTABILITY	post-observe-window instability alert (one source of app degraded)	Instability detected at runtime: check app logs to assess; the platform alerts once and advises manual rollback (no escalation counter).	release-semantics §2.7
W_DEPLOY_NO_HEALTHCHECK	0	https://docs.fleetly.dev/errors/W_DEPLOY_NO_HEALTHCHECK	service declares no healthcheck, health_gate=none (health gate skipped)	Add a healthcheck to the service; without one the health gate is skipped and the deploy passes straight through.	release-semantics §2.7/§2.8
W_ENV_PLATFORM_OVERRIDE	0	https://docs.fleetly.dev/errors/W_ENV_PLATFORM_OVERRIDE	platform-layer env_vars overrides same-named keys from files (three-layer merge chain)	Platform-layer env overrides same-named compose keys: the merge result follows the platform layer; check the platform env_vars.	architecture §2.4
W_PLACEMENT_STATELESS_PIN	0	https://docs.fleetly.dev/errors/W_PLACEMENT_STATELESS_PIN	stateless app auto-pinned because a new volume was added (data birthplace)	The stateless app was pinned because of the new volume: remove the volume declaration if free scheduling is needed.	stateful-placement §2.8
W_ROLLBACK_IMAGE_RISK	0	https://docs.fleetly.dev/errors/W_ROLLBACK_IMAGE_RISK	rollback target declared by tag; its content may have changed (not an immutable digest)	The rollback target image is declared by tag and its content may have changed: confirm the image content before replaying.	release-semantics §2.7
